---
import site from '../data/site.json';

const stages = [
  { n: '1', label: 'Bottle', detail: 'A clean, used PET drinking-water bottle.' },
  { n: '2', label: 'Filament', detail: 'Cut into a single continuous strand and re-formed at filament gauge on a Petamentor2 rebuild at ~185 °C, with the spool turning at ~1 rpm.' },
  { n: '3', label: 'Part', detail: 'Printed from the shrinkage-compensated hardware/rpet/ geometry instead of the standard STLs.' },
];
---
<section id="rpet">
  <div class="eyebrow">Recycled PET</div>
  <h2>Recycled PET filament</h2>
  <p class="lead">
    rPET, recycled from used drinking-water bottles, is one of five
    materials the manifold was tested in. The funnel and filter support
    can be printed in it directly.
  </p>

  <ol class="stages">
    {stages.map((s) => (
      <li>
        <span class="stage-n">{s.n}</span>
        <div>
          <div class="stage-label">{s.label}</div>
          <p class="stage-detail">{s.detail}</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <h3>Credit</h3>
  <p>
    The filament-making machine we used is our own rebuild of
    Petamentor2, an open-source PET-bottle-to-filament machine designed by
    Ondřej Šraitr
    (<a href="https://petamentor2.com/" rel="noopener">petamentor2.com</a>).
    We did not design the machine. Its design files are Šraitr's work, and
    this repository deliberately does not redistribute them. To build your
    own, use the upstream project.
  </p>

  <h3>Shrinkage-compensated geometry</h3>
  <p>
    rPET shrinks differently during cooling than ABS or PLA, so the parts
    in <code>hardware/rpet/</code> are dimensionally compensated for that
    shrinkage. Parts printed in rPET from the standard STLs will not fit.
    The base needs no compensation, so there is no separate rPET base. The
    same <code>hardware/stl/base.stl</code> is correct in every material,
    including rPET. rPET's print settings also differ enough from the ABS
    gas-tight profile that they do not carry over directly. See
    <a href={`${site.repo}/blob/main/docs/rpet.md`}>docs/rpet.md</a> for the
    settings source and the full bottle-to-filament procedure.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  #rpet h3 { margin: 28px 0 10px; }

  .stages {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 24px 0 32px;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 20px;
  }
  .stages li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 14px;
    padding: 20px;
    background: var(--bg-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  .stage-n {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 28px;
    color: var(--accent-2);
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .stage-label {
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .stage-detail {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  code {
    background: var(--bg-2);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: .92em;
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }

  @media (max-width: 780px) {
    .stages { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
